    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280">

                <pb facs="0421" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114 Supplies/4–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-11">April 11,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received April 11—9:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2125. American Interests—Far East—Relief supplies. Legation’s 6916, October
                        18,<anchor n="63" xml:id="d280-f1"/> Point <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sexto</hi>. Swiss note April 9 states Swiss Legation Tokyo telegraphed
                    April 5th as follows regarding transport of relief parcels and mail to Allied
                    POWs in Japanese hands: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>According communication from Japanese Foreign Office, Soviet Government
                            recently informed Japanese Government that it would authorize a Japanese
                            vessel to enter port of Nakhodka to load relief supplies under
                            conditions similar to those for the last transport. Japanese Government
                            has therefore decided to send vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Awa
                                Maru</hi> upon its return (Legation’s note: Please see Legation’s
                            1903, March 31<anchor n="64" xml:id="d280-f2"/>) and to proceed with
                            distribution of relief to prisoners of war and internees in the south
                            and other areas under the following conditions.</p>
                        <list>
                            <label>1.</label>
                            <item>Japan will assure the transport from Nakhodka under the same
                                conditions as those for transport on the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Hakusan Maru</hi> of approximately 2,200 tons of mail and
                                relief supplies stored or to be stored shortly on Soviet
                                territory.</item>
                            <label>2.</label>
                            <item>The United States will grant safe conduct for the <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Awa Maru</hi> as formerly for the <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Hakusan Maru</hi> and it will obtain
                                assurances of safe conduct of all interested countries including
                                Russia.</item>
                            <label>3.</label>
                            <item>The United States will similarly give safe conduct for the <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Awa Maru</hi> for the transport of relief
                                supplies to China and to the southern area as previously for the <hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Hosi Maru</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Awa Maru</hi>.</item>
                            <pb facs="0422" n="410" xml:id="pg410"/>
                            <label>4.</label>
                            <item>Japan will communicate to the Swiss Legation within the period
                                desired by the United States the route, schedule, departure and
                                characteristics of <hi rendition="#italic">Awa Maru</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Swiss Legation Tokyo adds that Japan prepared dispatch <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Awa Maru</hi> to Nakhodka middle of April.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d280-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
